From a94e7f52ba88e8c54872be286e4be35eecf2eac8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:37:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Native: the field menu's Item screen opens

Select, then Item, crashed the desktop build: ItemMenu_RunCommands hides
menu->selectedItemIcon before ItemMenu_SelectMember has made it, the first
time round. On the cartridge the null pointer's write lands in the BIOS,
which ignores it; natively it is a segfault. Under UBFIX (the native build)
the write is skipped while the icon is not there yet.

The GBA ROM is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ta8yjRdqf92zfRQjJVu8H
---
 games/tbs/src/menu/menu_item.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/games/tbs/src/menu/menu_item.c b/games/tbs/src/menu/menu_item.c
index 0af2dd1fc9..7a65a8fd41 100644
--- a/games/tbs/src/menu/menu_item.c
+++ b/games/tbs/src/menu/menu_item.c
@@ -232,7 +232,12 @@ s32 ItemMenu_RunCommands(s32 *memberOut, s32 *targetOut, s32 *itemOut) {
       menu->selectedSlots[0] = 0;
       ItemMenu_FitMessageWindowToQuestion();
       ItemMenu_PlaceItemWindowBelowQuestion();
-      menu->selectedItemIcon->motion = ICON_HIDDEN;
+      // The first time round, ItemMenu_SelectMember has not made the icon
+      // yet: the cartridge writes through the null pointer into the BIOS.
+#ifdef UBFIX
+      if (menu->selectedItemIcon != NULL)
+#endif
+        menu->selectedItemIcon->motion = ICON_HIDDEN;
       ItemMenu_DrawMessage(0, MsgWhoseItem);
 #if TBS_PATCH_1
       WindowSprite_RedrawSavedRectFar(menu->descriptionWindow);
